WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.862
The roadmap sequences all of this as an
illustrative fifty-two-week program.

2
00:00:04.862 --> 00:00:08.000
The weeks are a sequencing
model, not a commitment;

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.062
large federal estates
typically run multi-year.

4
00:00:11.062 --> 00:00:13.399
There are seven phases and six gates.

5
00:00:13.399 --> 00:00:17.232
Phase 0, pre-flight, stands
up the platform host

6
00:00:17.232 --> 00:00:20.762
and runs the assessment;
G0 is Ready to Plan.

7
00:00:20.762 --> 00:00:25.051
Phase 1, foundation, puts the
identity primitives in place,

8
00:00:25.051 --> 00:00:30.412
including the access baseline and the
HR feed; G1 is Foundation Complete.

9
00:00:30.412 --> 00:00:34.556
Phase 2 proves the whole
pattern on one pilot division,

10
00:00:34.556 --> 00:00:39.251
typically IT; G2, Pilot Clean,
needs zero drift for a hold period.

11
00:00:39.251 --> 00:00:44.950
Phase 3, the longest, rolls out division
by division, two or three at a time.

12
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:48.851
Phase 4 retires legacy
policy, groups, DNS,

13
00:00:48.851 --> 00:00:54.587
DHCP and the last service principal
names; G4 is Legacy Quiet.

14
00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:58.624
Phase 5, the shortest, retires AD DS.

15
00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:00.850
And Phase 6 is steady state.

16
00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:02.487
Two properties define it.

17
00:01:02.487 --> 00:01:07.377
The five workstreams, identity,
policy, services, compute and access,

18
00:01:07.377 --> 00:01:10.084
run in parallel, each with a named lead;

19
00:01:10.084 --> 00:01:14.537
finishing one before starting
the next doubles the duration.

20
00:01:14.537 --> 00:01:18.837
And it's gated: a phase opens only
when the previous gate clears.

21
00:01:18.837 --> 00:01:21.726
The decision closes the loop on ownership.

22
00:01:21.726 --> 00:01:24.280
Put the gate dates on
the sponsor's calendar,

23
00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:28.113
and the end date of every exception
on the authorizing official's.

24
00:01:28.113 --> 00:01:31.320
Gate G0 gets its date in Phase 0.
